/** Standalone batch AN -- new 4-case standard (Sample + boundary + tricky + stress).
 * All solvers below were independently written and verified byte-for-byte against each problem's
 * real official Sample before being trusted to generate boundary/tricky/stress expected output.
 *
 * uva-12918-lucky-thief: closed-form identification-cost formula answer = n*m - n*(n+1)/2, derived by
 *   pattern-matching against the real sample's own n==m cases (which reduce to the pure triangular-
 *   number n*(n-1)/2) and confirmed against every other dataset. Verified against all 20 datasets in
 *   the real sample.
 * uva-12911-subset-sum: classic meet-in-the-middle (N<=40 splits into two <=20-element halves, each
 *   enumerated as all 2^20 subset sums, then matched via a hash map), subtracting 1 for the T==0 case
 *   to exclude the empty+empty (fully non-empty-violating) pair. Verified against the problem
 *   statement's own two worked examples and the full real sample (18 datasets).
 * uva-12869-zeroes: since f_zero(v)-f_zero(v-1) equals v's 5-adic valuation (0 unless v is a multiple
 *   of 5, in which case it can be >1) -- so f_zero only ever "jumps" at multiples of 5, but importantly
 *   each such jump (regardless of its SIZE) contributes exactly ONE new distinct value to the achieved-
 *   value set -- the count of distinct outputs over v in [low,high] is simply 1 + (multiples of 5 in
 *   (low,high]) = floor(high/5) - floor(low/5) + 1. Uses BigInt throughout since high can reach 9*10^18,
 *   beyond safe-integer range. Verified against the problem statement's own worked example (1 to 10 ->
 *   3 distinct values) and the full real sample.
 * uva-13055-inception: direct stack simulation (Sleep pushes, Kick pops if non-empty per the problem's
 *   own explicit "ignore if not in anyone's dream" rule, Test reports the top or "Not in a dream").
 *   Verified against the real sample's full 59-query trace.
 * uva-13171-pixel-art: reverse-engineered the non-primary color compositions (not given as an explicit
 *   table in the OCR'd statement) by solving for consistency against the real sample's own paint-
 *   remainder outputs: R=magenta+yellow, G=yellow+cyan, V=magenta+cyan, B=all three, W=none -- cross-
 *   verified against two independent sample datasets that isolate green and violet respectively.
 *   Verified against all 14 datasets in the real sample.
 * uva-12592-slogan-learning-of-princess: direct hash-map lookup from first line to second line; a
 *   fully general line-based parser is required since slogans contain spaces (using \s+ token
 *   splitting would corrupt them). Verified against all 16 real-sample queries.
 * uva-13204-count-these-permutations: the maximum possible total displacement of a length-n permutation
 *   is the well-known floor(n^2/2), and the count of permutations achieving it was pattern-matched
 *   against the real sample as (n/2)!^2 for even n, or n*((n-1)/2)!^2 for odd n (derived by comparing
 *   consecutive odd/even outputs against factorial-squared ratios) -- verified against all 10 datasets
 *   in the real sample, including the large n=999999 case (via precomputed factorials mod 1e9+7).
 */
